# Ingestion pipeline

Entry: Celery `process_document(doc_id)`. Status: `pending → processing → ready | failed` with `last_error` on failure.

## Extraction

- Open PDF with PyMuPDF (`fitz`). Keep **physical page numbers**.
- Extract text per page. If a table grid is detected, extract with pdfplumber as GitHub-flavored Markdown (`| col | col |`).
- Preserve coordinates when available — the PDF viewer highlight depends on them later.

## Chunking (not naive RAG)

- A chunk **must not cross a page boundary**. Prefer section boundaries when headings exist.
- Size: 400–600 tokens, overlap: 50 tokens, overlap only within the same page/section.
- Prefix every chunk **before** embedding (`chunker.format_embed_text`):

```
[Document: HR_Policy.pdf | Section: Expenses | Page: 12]
{content}
```

- `document_chunks.content` is the fragment **without** that header (UI, LLM, citation snippet). `embed_text` is computed at embed time, not stored as a column.
- Payload must include: `document_id`, `organization_id` (copy from the document row, M5), `chunk_id`, `page_number`, `section_title`, `is_table`, `access_roles`, `content`, `token_count`.

## Embed & upsert

- Batch `fastembed` dense vectors (`BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5`, 384d cosine) from `embed_text`.
- Delete existing rows for `document_id` before insert (replace, do not duplicate).
- Index `document_id`, `organization_id` (M5), and GIN on `access_roles`; HNSW on `embedding`.
- Copy `access_roles` and `organization_id` from the parent document at ingest time; `PATCH /documents/{id}` updates document **and** chunk ACL rows (no re-embed; org does not change).

## Tests to keep green

Upload a PDF that contains a table; assert chunks stay on one page, tables survive as Markdown, and payload `access_roles` match the document.
